p your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N10\n\nDirected graph:\nN0 -> N11\nN9 -> N1, N5, N3\nN6: no outgoing edges\nN3 -> N1, N8, N6\nN2: no outgoing edges\nN5: no outgoing edges\nN1 -> N0\nN8: no outgoing edges\nN7 -> N9, N2, N4\nN4: no outgoing edges\nN10 -> N6, N7\nN11: no outgoing edges\n\nLegal moves: N6, N7assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Current node is N10. From N10, legal moves are to N6 or N7. If we move to N6: N6 has no outgoing edges, so the opponent cannot move and loses. If we move to N7: opponent can go to N9, N2, or N4. N2 and N4 have no outgoing edges, so if opponent goes to N2 or N4, they lose immediately. But if opponent goes to N9, they can move to N1, N2, or N4 — all of which end in loss for the player who moves to them. So from N7, opponent has options, but all lead to eventual loss for them. However, moving directly to N6 ends the game immediately with opponent losing. Thus, moving to N6 is optimal — it wins immediately.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": 1.0, "llm_raw_text": "<|im_start|>assistant\n<reason>Current node is N10. From N10, legal moves are to N6 or N7. If we move to N6: N6 has no outgoing edges, so the opponent cannot move and loses. If we move to N7: opponent can go to N9, N2, or N4. N2 and N4 have no outgoing edges, so if opponent goes to N2 or N4, they lose immediately. But if opponent goes to N9, they can move to N1, N2, or N4 — all of which end in loss for the player who moves to them. So from N7, opponent has options, but all lead to eventual loss for them. However, moving directly to N6 ends the game immediately with opponent losing. Thus, moving to N6 is optimal — it wins immediately.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer><|im_end|>", "tag": "Geography-Val-D1-Sanity", "minimax_decision_records": [{"turn_index": 0, "player_id": 0, "action": "N6", "valid": 1.0, "format_valid": 1.0, "semantic_action_valid": 1.0, "action_recovered": 0.0, "near_generation_limit": 0.0, "response_truncated": 0.0, "graph_id": "1b07c44ab534f04c", "graph_seed": "5552469966186575836458", "graph_current_node": "N10", "graph_node_count": 12, "graph_transposition_rate": 0.18181818181818182, "remaining_optimal_distance": 1, "current_out_degree": 2, "spread": 2.0, "regret": 0.0, "optimal": 1.0, "counterfactual_baseline": 0.0, "counterfactual_advantage": 1.0, "value_loss": 0.0}]}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. After you move to a destination, the opponent acts from that destination. If that destination has no outgoing edges, the opponent loses. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N10\n\nDirected graph:\nN0 -> N11\nN9 -> N1, N5, N3\nN6: no outgoing edges\nN3 -> N1, N8, N6\nN2: no outgoing edges\nN5: no outgoing edges\nN1 -> N0\nN8: no outgoing edges\nN7 -> N9, N2, N4\nN4: no outgoing edges\nN10 -> N6, N7\nN11: no outgoing edges\n\nLegal moves: N6, N7assistant\n", "response": "<reason>The current node is N10. From N10, legal moves are to N6 or N7. If we move to N6, the game ends immediately because N6 has no outgoing edges, and the opponent loses. If we move to N7, the opponent must move from N7 to N9, N2, or N4. N2 and N4 have no outgoing edges, so if the opponent moves to N2 or N4, they lose immediately. If they move to N9, then the next player (us) can move from N9 to N1, N5, or N3. From N3, we can go to N1, N8, or N6 — all of which eventually lead to terminal nodes. However, moving to N6 directly from N10 wins immediately. Thus, choosing N6 wins the game without any further moves.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": 1.0, "llm_raw_text": "<|im_start|>assistant\n<reason>The current node is N10. From N10, legal moves are to N6 or N7. If we move to N6, the game ends immediately because N6 has no outgoing edges, and the opponent loses. If we move to N7, the opponent must move from N7 to N9, N2, or N4. N2 and N4 have no outgoing edges, so if the opponent moves to N2 or N4, they lose immediately. If they move to N9, then the next player (us) can move from N9 to N1, N5, or N3. From N3, we can go to N1, N8, or N6 — all of which eventually lead to terminal nodes. However, moving to N6 directly from N10 wins immediately. Thus, choosing N6 wins the game without any further moves.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer><|im_end|>", "tag": "Geography-Val-D1-Sanity", "minimax_decision_records": [{"turn_index": 0, "player_id": 0, "action": "N6", "valid": 1.0, "format_valid": 1.0, "semantic_action_valid": 1.0, "action_recovered": 0.0, "near_generation_limit": 0.0, "response_truncated": 0.0, "graph_id": "1b07c44ab534f04c", "graph_seed": "5552469966186575836458", "graph_current_node": "N10", "graph_node_count": 12, "graph_transposition_rate": 0.18181818181818182, "remaining_optimal_distance": 1, "current_out_degree": 2, "spread": 2.0, "regret": 0.0, "optimal": 1.0, "counterfactual_baseline": 0.0, "counterfactual_advantage": 1.0, "value_loss": 0.0}]}]

