.  \n  - N9 → N7 or N6.  \n    - N7 has no outgoing edges → opponent loses.  \n    - N6 → N1 or N0 (both terminal).  \n  So from N3, opponent eventually faces a terminal node.  \n- Moving to N10: leads to N5 or N8.  \n  - N8 has no outgoing edges → opponent loses immediately.  \n  - N5 → N7 or N2.  \n    - N7: terminal → opponent loses.  \n    - N2 → N1 or N11 (both terminal).  \nSo both N3 and N10 lead to opponent losing eventually. However, N10 leads to immediate loss of opponent via N8. This is a winning move. Since the goal is to maximize outcome, and reaching a terminal node for opponent is optimal, choosing N10 ensures immediate win. Thus, N10 is better than N3.</reason>\n<answer>N10</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Current node is N13. From N13, legal moves are to N3 or N10.  \n- Moving to N3: leads to N4 or N9.  \n  - N4 → N0 or N12 (both terminal, opponent loses).  \n  - N9 → N7 or N6.  \n    - N7 has no outgoing edges → opponent loses.  \n    - N6 → N1 or N0 (both terminal).  \n  So from N3, opponent eventually faces a terminal node.  \n- Moving to N10: leads to N5 or N8.  \n  - N8 has no outgoing edges → opponent loses immediately.  \n  - N5 → N7 or N2.  \n    - N7: terminal → opponent loses.  \n    - N2 → N1 or N11 (both terminal).  \nSo both N3 and N10 lead to opponent losing eventually. However, N10 leads to immediate loss of opponent via N8. This is a winning move. Since the goal is to maximize outcome, and reaching a terminal node for opponent is optimal, choosing N10 ensures immediate win. Thus, N10 is better than N3.</reason>\n<answer>N10</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. After you move to a destination, the opponent acts from that destination. If that destination has no outgoing edges, the opponent loses. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game ou