[2026-08-18 11:45:30] [agentic_pipeline.py (561)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 1863312] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. After you move to a destination, the opponent acts from that destination. If that destination has no outgoing edges, the opponent loses. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N12\n\nDirected graph:\nN7: no outgoing edges\nN10 -> N2\nN5 -> N0\nN12 -> N4, N3, N5\nN4 -> N3\nN0: no outgoing edges\nN13 -> N6, N9, N10\nN3 -> N11, N13, N7\nN11 -> N1\nN8: no outgoing edges\nN2: no outgoing edges\nN1: no outgoing edges\nN6 -> N8, N9, N11\nN9: no outgoing edges\n\nLegal moves: N4, N3, N5assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N12, legal moves are to N4, N3, or N5. We analyze each:\n\n- N4 → N3 → N11 → N1 (terminal; opponent loses after N1, which has no outgoing edges). After N4, opponent moves to N3, then to N11, then to N1 (no outgoing edges), so opponent loses. So we win.\n\n- N3 → N11 → N1 (same path), opponent loses. So winning.\n\n- N5 → N0 (no outgoing edges), opponent loses immediately. So this is also a win.\n\nAll moves lead to opponent losing. But we want to maximize outcome. Since all moves result in win, we pick one. N5 leads to immediate loss for opponent (N0), which is optimal. So choose N5.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N12, legal moves are to N4, N3, or N5. We analyze each:\n\n- N4 → N3 → N11 → N1 (terminal; opponent loses after N1, which has no outgoing edges). After N4, opponent moves to N3, then to N11, then to N1 (no outgoing edges), so opponent loses. So we win.\n\n- N3 → N11 → N1 (same path), opponent loses. So winning.\n\n- N5 → N0 (no outgoing edges), opponent loses immediately. So this is also a win.\n\nAll moves lead to opponent losing. But we want to maximize outcome. Since all moves result in win, we pick one. N5 leads to immediate loss for opponent (N0), which is optimal. So choose N5.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. After you move to a destination, the opponent acts from that destination. If that destination has no outgoing edges, the opponent loses. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N12\n\nDirected graph:\nN7: no outgoing edges\nN10 -> N2\nN5 -> N0\nN12 -> N4, N3, N5\nN4 -> N3\nN0: no outgoing edges\nN13 -> N6, N9, N10\nN3 -> N11, N13, N7\nN11 -> N1\nN8: no outgoing edges\nN2: no outgoing edges\nN1: no outgoing edges\nN6 -> N8, N9, N11\nN9: no outgoing edges\n\nLegal moves: N4, N3, N5assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N12, the legal moves are to N4, N3, or N5. We analyze each:\n\n- N4 → N3 → N11 → N1 (then no moves), then opponent moves from N1 (no outgoing edges) → opponent loses. So if we go to N4, then opponent is at N3, which leads to N11 → N1 (no outgoing), so opponent loses. This is a win.\n\n- N3 → N11 → N1 (no moves), then opponent at N1 (no outgoing) → opponent loses. So going to N3 is also a win.\n\n- N5 → N0 (no outgoing), opponent at N0 → opponent loses. So going to N5 is also a win.\n\nAll moves lead to opponent losing immediately. But we want to maximize outcome — since all lead to win, any is valid. However, N5 leads to immediate end (N0 has no outgoing), so opponent loses right 