[2026-08-18 11:52:50] [agentic_pipeline.py (561)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 1863312] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. After you move to a destination, the opponent acts from that destination. If that destination has no outgoing edges, the opponent loses. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N0\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> N8, N5\nN5: no outgoing edges\nN9 -> N7, N4\nN3: no outgoing edges\nN6: no outgoing edges\nN8 -> N3\nN4 -> N6, N5\nN0 -> N9, N2\nN1: no outgoing edges\nN2 -> N4, N1\n\nLegal moves: N9, N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N0, legal moves are to N9 or N2.  \n- Moving to N9: next player faces N9 → N7 or N4.  \n  - N7 → N8 → N3 (loss for next player).  \n  - N4 → N6 (loss) or N5 (loss). So both paths lead to opponent losing immediately.  \n  Thus, from N9, opponent loses no matter what.  \n- Moving to N2: next player faces N2 → N4 or N1.  \n  - N4 → N6 or N5 (both terminal, opponent loses).  \n  - N1: no outgoing edges → opponent loses immediately.  \n  So from N2, opponent also loses immediately.  \n\nBoth N9 and N2 lead to opponent losing immediately. Either move wins. Choose one. N9 is earlier in the graph and leads to a forced win. Choose N9.</reason>  \n<answer>N9</answer>", "episode_score": 1.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N0, legal moves are to N9 or N2.  \n- Moving to N9: next player faces N9 → N7 or N4.  \n  - N7 → N8 → N3 (loss for next player).  \n  - N4 → N6 (loss) or N5 (loss). So both paths lead to opponent losing immediately.  \n  Thus, from N9, opponent loses no matter what.  \n- Moving to N2: next player faces N2 → N4 or N1.  \n  - N4 → N6 or N5 (both terminal, opponent loses).  \n  - N1: no outgoing edges → opponent loses immediately.  \n  So from N2, opponent also loses immediately.  \n\nBoth N9 and N2 lead to opponent losing immediately. Either move wins. Choose one. N9 is earlier in the graph and leads to a forced win. Choose N9.</reason>  \n<answer>N9</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. After you move to a destination, the opponent acts from that destination. If that destination has no outgoing edges, the opponent loses. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N0\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> N8, N5\nN5: no outgoing edges\nN9 -> N7, N4\nN3: no outgoing edges\nN6: no outgoing edges\nN8 -> N3\nN4 -> N6, N5\nN0 -> N9, N2\nN1: no outgoing edges\nN2 -> N4, N1\n\nLegal moves: N9, N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N0, legal moves are to N9 or N2.  \n- Moving to N9: next player faces N9 → N7 or N4.  \n  - N7 → N8 → N3 (opponent loses). So N7 is a winning move.  \n  - N4 → N6 (dead end) or N5 (dead end). Both lose for opponent.  \n  So from N9, opponent can go to N7 (win) or N4 (lose). If opponent chooses N7, they win. So N9 is risky.  \n- Moving to N2: next player faces N2 → N4 or N1.  \n  - N1: dead end → opponent loses.  \n  - N4 → N6 or N5 (both dead ends).  \n  So from N2, opponent can choose N1 (they lose immediately) or N4 (they lose). So opponent loses no matter what.  \nThus, moving to N2 forces opponent into a losing position. This is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N0, legal moves ar