[2026-08-18 12:02:38] [agentic_pipeline.py (561)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 1863312] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. After you move to a destination, the opponent acts from that destination. If that destination has no outgoing edges, the opponent loses. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN0 -> N1\nN1 -> N2\nN9 -> N3, N5\nN8 -> N6, N9\nN3: no outgoing edges\nN7: no outgoing edges\nN5 -> N6, N7\nN2: no outgoing edges\nN6: no outgoing edges\nN4 -> N8, N0, N1\n\nLegal moves: N8, N0, N1assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Current node is N4. From N4, legal moves are to N8, N0, or N1. We analyze each:\n\n- Move to N8: Next player faces N8, which has edges to N6 and N9.\n  - From N8 → N6: N6 has no outgoing edges → opponent loses → we win.\n  - From N8 → N9: N9 → N3 or N5.\n    - N3: no outgoing edges → opponent loses → we win.\n    - N5 → N6 or N7; both end with no outgoing edges → opponent loses → we win.\n  → All moves from N8 lead to opponent losing.\n\n- Move to N0: Next player faces N0 → N1 → N2 (no outgoing edges) → opponent loses → we win.\n\n- Move to N1: Next player faces N1 → N2 (no outgoing edges) → opponent loses → we win.\n\nAll moves lead to opponent losing. Since the goal is to maximize outcome, any move wins. Choose one. Pick N8 as it offers the most branching and ensures a win regardless of opponent's choice.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Current node is N4. From N4, legal moves are to N8, N0, or N1. We analyze each:\n\n- Move to N8: Next player faces N8, which has edges to N6 and