[2026-08-18 12:04:30] [agentic_pipeline.py (561)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 1863312] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. After you move to a destination, the opponent acts from that destination. If that destination has no outgoing edges, the opponent loses. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N3\n\nDirected graph:\nN5 -> N8, N2\nN7: no outgoing edges\nN9: no outgoing edges\nN0: no outgoing edges\nN6 -> N0, N4\nN3 -> N2, N5, N6\nN8 -> N7, N9\nN1: no outgoing edges\nN2 -> N8\nN4 -> N1\n\nLegal moves: N2, N5, N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N3, legal moves are to N2, N5, or N6. We analyze each:\n\n- Move to N2: goes to N2 → N8 → N7 or N9 (both terminal). Opponent wins immediately.\n- Move to N5: goes to N5 → N8 → N7 or N9. Opponent wins.\n- Move to N6: goes to N6 → N0 or N4.  \n  - N0: terminal → opponent loses.  \n  - N4 → N1: terminal → opponent loses.  \nSo from N6, either path ends with opponent losing. Thus, moving to N6 forces opponent into a terminal node.\n\nAll other moves lead to opponent winning. Only N6 leads to opponent losing. Therefore, N6 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N3, legal moves are to N2, N5, or N6. We analyze each:\n\n- Move to N2: goes to N2 → N8 → N7 or N9 (both terminal). Opponent wins immediately.\n- Move to N5: goes to N5 → N8 → N7 or N9. Opponent wins.\n- Move to N6: goes to N6 → N0 or N4.  \n  - N0: terminal → opponent loses.  \n  - N4 → N1: terminal → opponent loses.  \nSo from N6, either path ends with opponent losing. Thus, moving to N6 forces opponent into a terminal node.\n\nAll other moves lead to opponent winning. Only N6 leads to opponent losing. Therefore, N6 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. After you move to a destination, the opponent acts from that destination. If that destination has no outgoing edges, the opponent loses. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N3\n\nDirected graph:\nN5 -> N8, N2\nN7: no outgoing edges\nN9: no outgoing edges\nN0: no outgoing edges\nN6 -> N0, N4\nN3 -> N2, N5, N6\nN8 -> N7, N9\nN1: no outgoing edges\nN2 -> N8\nN4 -> N1\n\nLegal moves: N2, N5, N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N3, legal moves are to N2, N5, or N6. We analyze each:\n\n- Move to N2: goes to N2 → N8 → N7 or N9 (both dead ends). Opponent wins immediately after their move to N7 or N9. So we lose.\n\n- Move to N5: goes to N5 → N8 → N7 or N9. Again, opponent wins after their move. Loss.\n\n- Move to N6: goes to N6 → N0 or N4.  \n  - If to N0: dead end → opponent loses.  \n  - If to N4: goes to N4 → N1 (dead end) → opponent loses.  \n  So from N6, opponent has no legal move and loses.\n\nThus, moving to N6 leads to opponent's loss. This is the only winning move.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N3, legal moves are to N2, N5, or N6. We analyze each:\n\n- Move to N2: goes to N2 → N8 → N7 or N9 (both dead ends). Opponent wins immediately after their move to N7 or N9. So we lose.\n\n- Move to N5: goes to N5 → N8 → N7 or N9. Again, opponent wins after their move. Loss.\n\n- Move to N6: goes to N6 → N0 or N4.  \n  - If to N0: 