[2026-08-18 12:13:40] [agentic_pipeline.py (561)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 1863312] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. After you move to a destination, the opponent acts from that destination. If that destination has no outgoing edges, the opponent loses. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N8\n\nDirected graph:\nN5 -> N0, N9\nN1: no outgoing edges\nN12 -> N5, N13, N1\nN9: no outgoing edges\nN10 -> N11\nN7 -> N12\nN4: no outgoing edges\nN13 -> N3, N4, N2\nN2: no outgoing edges\nN8 -> N5, N7, N10\nN0 -> N4, N6\nN6: no outgoing edges\nN3 -> N6\nN11: no outgoing edges\n\nLegal moves: N5, N7, N10assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N8, legal moves are to N5, N7, or N10. We analyze each:\n\n- Move to N5: leads to N0 or N9. N9 is terminal (opponent loses). N0 leads to N4 or N6, both terminal. So opponent eventually loses. Good outcome.\n\n- Move to N7: leads to N12. From N12, options are N5, N13, N1. N1 is terminal. N5 → N0/N9 (N9 terminal). N13 → N3 → N6 (terminal). All paths eventually end with opponent losing. Good.\n\n- Move to N10: leads to N11 (terminal). Opponent loses immediately. This is the best outcome — immediate win.\n\nThus, moving to N10 results in opponent having no move and losing immediately. This is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N10</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N8, legal moves are to N5, N7, or N10. We analyze each:\n\n- Move to N5: leads to N0 or N9. N9 is terminal (opponent loses). N0 leads to N4 or N6, both terminal. So opponent eventually loses. Good outcome.\n\n- Move to N7: leads to N12. From N12, options are N5, N13, N1. N1 is terminal. N5 → N0/N9 (N9 terminal). N13 → N3 → N6 (terminal). All paths eventually end with opponent losing. Good.\n\n- Move to N10: leads to N11 (terminal). Opponent loses immediately. This is the best outcome — immediate win.\n\nThus, moving to N10 results in opponent having no move and losing immediately. This is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N10</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. After you move to a destination, the opponent acts from that destination. If that destination has no outgoing edges, the opponent loses. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N8\n\nDirected graph:\nN5 -> N0, N9\nN1: no outgoing edges\nN12 -> N5, N13, N1\nN9: no outgoing edges\nN10 -> N11\nN7 -> N12\nN4: no outgoing edges\nN13 -> N3, N4, N2\nN2: no outgoing edges\nN8 -> N5, N7, N10\nN0 -> N4, N6\nN6: no outgoing edges\nN3 -> N6\nN11: no outgoing edges\n\nLegal moves: N5, N7, N10assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N8, legal moves are to N5, N7, or N10.  \n- Moving to N5: leads to N0 or N9. N9 is terminal (opponent loses), N0 leads to N4 or N6 (both terminal). So opponent loses immediately if we go to N9 or N0→N9.  \n- Moving to N7: leads to N12, which leads to N5, N13, or N1. N1 is terminal, so opponent can go to N13 → N3 → N6 (terminal) or N4 → terminal, or N2 → terminal. All paths eventually end.  \n- Moving to N10: leads to N11 (terminal), so opponent loses immediately.  \n\nBest outcome: N10 leads directly to a terminal node (N11), so opponent has no move and loses. This is a winning move.  \nThus, N10 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N10</answer>", "episode_s