 leads directly to N7 (immediate loss for opponent), it is optimal to choose the move that gives immediate loss. N3 → N7 is simplest and guarantees opponent loses on their turn. Thus, N3 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N5, legal moves are to N9, N3, or N0.  \n- N9 → N1 → N8 → N6 (N6 has no outgoing edges, so opponent loses after opponent moves from N6). So N9 leads to opponent's loss.  \n- N3 → N7 (N7 has no outgoing edges, so opponent loses immediately).  \n- N0 → N3 → N7 (same as above: opponent loses after their move from N7).  \n\nAll moves lead to opponent losing on their next turn. However, we must choose the one that maximizes our outcome. Since all lead to opponent losing, any move is equivalent in outcome. But N9 leads to N1 → N8 → N6, which is a longer path, and N3 or N0 both lead directly to N7. Since N3 leads directly to N7 (immediate loss for opponent), it is optimal to choose the move that gives immediate loss. N3 → N7 is simplest and guarantees opponent loses on their turn. Thus, N3 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. After you move to a destination, the opponent acts from that destination. If that destination has no outgoing edges, the opponent loses. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N2\n\nDirected graph:\nN4 -> N7, N5\nN8: no outgoing edges\nN9 -> N4\nN2 -> N7, N9, N0\nN6: no outgoing edges\nN5: no outgoing edges\nN7 -> N8\nN0 -> N1, N6\nN1 -> N3, N9\nN3: no outgoing edges\n\nLegal moves: N7, N9, N0assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N2, legal moves are to N7, N9, or N0.  \n- Moving to N7: goes to N7 → N8 (opponent's turn at N8, which has no outgoing edges → opponent loses → I win).  \n- Moving to N9: goes to N9 → N4 → N7 → N8 (opponent loses).  \n- Moving to N0: goes to N0 → N1 or N6. If to N1: N1 → N3 (no outgoing) or N9 → N4 → N7 → N8. Either way, opponent eventually faces N8 and loses. If to N6: opponent loses immediately. So N0 leads to opponent losing.  \n\nAll moves lead to opponent losing. But we want to maximize outcome — any move wins. Since all are winning, pick one. N7 is simplest and directly leads to opponent losing at N8. Choose N7.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N2, legal moves are to N7, N9, or N0.  \n- Moving to N7: goes to N7 → N8 (opponent's turn at N8, which has no outgoing edges → opponent loses → I win).  \n- Moving to N9: goes to N9 → N4 → N7 → N8 (opponent loses).  \n- Moving to N0: goes to N0 → N1 or N6. If to N1: N1 → N3 (no outgoing) or N9 → N4 → N7 → N8. Either way, opponent eventually faces N8 and loses. If to N6: opponent loses immediately. So N0 leads to opponent losing.  \n\nAll moves lead to opponent losing. But we want to maximize outcome — any move wins. Since all are winning, pick one. N7 is simplest and directly leads to opponent losing at N8. Choose N7.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. After you move to a destination, the opponent acts from that destination. If that destination has no outgoing edges, the opponent loses. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N2\n\nDirected 