[2026-08-18 12:30:43] [agentic_pipeline.py (561)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 1863312] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. After you move to a destination, the opponent acts from that destination. If that destination has no outgoing edges, the opponent loses. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N3\n\nDirected graph:\nN9 -> N0\nN11 -> N4, N9\nN7: no outgoing edges\nN2 -> N8, N7\nN6 -> N13\nN8: no outgoing edges\nN1: no outgoing edges\nN0 -> N2, N1\nN12 -> N6, N10\nN4 -> N12, N9\nN10: no outgoing edges\nN13: no outgoing edges\nN5 -> N4, N11\nN3 -> N5, N2\n\nLegal moves: N5, N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N3, the legal moves are to N5 or N2.  \n- Moving to N5: leads to N4 or N11.  \n  - N4 → N12 or N9; N12 → N6 or N10; N6 → N13 (terminal, opponent loses).  \n  - N9 → N0 → N2 or N1; N2 → N8 (terminal) or N7 (terminal).  \n  - All paths from N5 eventually lead to terminal nodes (no outgoing edges) for the opponent.  \n- Moving to N2: leads to N8 (terminal) or N7 (terminal). Opponent loses immediately.  \n\nThus, moving to N2 results in an immediate win. This is a better outcome than any path from N5.  \n</reason>  \n<answer>N2</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N3, the legal moves are to N5 or N2.  \n- Moving to N5: leads to N4 or N11.  \n  - N4 → N12 or N9; N12 → N6 or N10; N6 → N13 (terminal, opponent loses).  \n  - N9 → N0 → N2 or N1; N2 → N8 (terminal) or N7 (terminal).  \n  - All paths from N5 eventually lead to terminal nodes (no outgoing edges) for the opponent.  \n- Moving to N2: leads to N8 (terminal) or N7 (terminal). Opponent loses immediately.  \n\nThus, moving to N2 results in an immediate win. This is a better outcome than any path from N5.  \n</reason>  \n<answer>N2</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. After you move to a destination, the opponent acts from that destination. If that destination has no outgoing edges, the opponent loses. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N3\n\nDirected graph:\nN9 -> N0\nN11 -> N4, N9\nN7: no outgoing edges\nN2 -> N8, N7\nN6 -> N13\nN8: no outgoing edges\nN1: no outgoing edges\nN0 -> N2, N1\nN12 -> N6, N10\nN4 -> N12, N9\nN10: no outgoing edges\nN13: no outgoing edges\nN5 -> N4, N11\nN3 -> N5, N2\n\nLegal moves: N5, N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N3, the legal moves are to N5 or N2.  \n- Moving to N5: leads to N4 or N11.  \n  - N4 → N12 or N9; N12 → N6 or N10; N6 → N13 (terminal, opponent loses).  \n  - N9 → N0 → N2 or N1; N2 → N8 (terminal) or N7 (terminal).  \n  - This path can lead to terminal nodes for opponent.  \n- Moving to N2: leads to N8 (terminal) or N7 (terminal). Both are terminal, so opponent loses immediately.  \n\nThus, moving to N2 ends the game immediately with opponent losing. This is a winning move.  \nN5 leads to longer paths but does not guarantee immediate win. N2 gives immediate win.  \nTherefore, N2 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N3, the legal moves are to N5 or N2.  \n- Moving to N5: leads to N4 or N11.  \n  - N4 → N12 or N9; N12 → N6 or N10; N6 → N13 (terminal, opponent loses).  \n  - N9 → N0 → N2 or N1; N2 → N8 (terminal) or N7 (terminal).  \n  - This path can lead to terminal nodes for opponent.  \n- Moving to N2: leads to N8 (terminal) or N7 (terminal). Both are terminal, so opponent loses immediately.  \n\nThus, moving to N2 ends the game immediately with opponent losing. This is a winning move.  \nN5 leads to longer paths but does not guarantee immediate win. N2 gives immediate win.  \nTherefore, N2 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. After you move to a destination, the opponent acts from that destination. If that destination has no outgoing edges, the opponent loses. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N3\n\nDirected graph:\nN9 -> N0\nN11 -> N4, N9\nN7: no outgoing edges\nN2 -> N8, N7\nN6 -> N13\nN8: no outgoing edges\nN1: no outgoing edges\nN0 -> N2, N1\nN12 -> N6, N10\nN4 -> N12, N9\nN10: no outgoing edges\nN13: no outgoing edges\nN5 -> N4, N11\nN3 -> N5, N2\n\nLegal moves: N5, N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N3, the legal moves are to N5 or N2.  \n- Moving to N5: leads to N4 or N11.  \n  - N4 → N12 or N9; N12 → N6 or N10; N6 → N13 (terminal, opponent loses).  \n  - N9 → N0 → N2 or N1; N2 → N8 (terminal) or N7 (terminal).  \n  - All paths from N5 eventually lead to terminal nodes (no outgoing edges) for the opponent.  \n- Moving to N2: leads to N8 (terminal) or N7 (terminal). Both are terminal, so opponent loses immediately.  \n\nBoth moves end with opponent losing, but moving to N2 ends the game immediately. Moving to N5 allows more options but still ends with opponent losing. Since N2 results in immediate opponent loss and is a winning move, it is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N3, the legal moves are to N5 or N2.  \n- Moving to N5: leads to N4 or N11.  \n  - N4 → N12 or N9; N12 → N6 or N10; N6 → N13 (terminal, opponent loses).  \n  - N9 → N0 → N2 or N1; N2 → N8 (terminal) or N7 (terminal).  \n  - All paths from N5 eventually lead to terminal nodes (no outgoing edges) for the opponent.  \n- Moving to N2: leads to N8 (terminal) or N7 (terminal). Both are terminal, so opponent loses immediately.  \n\nBoth moves end with opponent losing, but moving to N2 ends the game immediately. Moving to N5 allows more options but still ends with opponent losing. Since N2 results in immediate opponent loss and is a winning move, it is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. After you move to a destination, the opponent acts from that destination. If that destination has no outgoing edges, the opponent loses. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N3\n\nDirected graph:\nN9 -> N0\nN11 -> N4, N9\nN7: no outgoing edges\nN2 -> N8, N7\nN6 -> N13\nN8: no outgoing edges\nN1: no outgoing edges\nN0 -> N2, N1\nN12 -> N6, N10\nN4 -> N12, N9\nN10: no outgoing edges\nN13: no outgoing edges\nN5 -> N4, N11\nN3 -> N5, N2\n\nLegal moves: N5, N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Current node is N3. From N3, legal moves are to N5 or N2.  \n- Moving to N5: next node is N4 or N11.  \n  - N4 leads to N12 or N9.  \n    - N12 → N6 or N10; N6 → N13 (terminal), N10 (terminal).  \n    - N9 → N0 → N2 or