1, N5\nN0: no outgoing edges\nN12: no outgoing edges\nN13 -> N11, N3, N10\nN6: no outgoing edges\nN5 -> N7\n\nLegal moves: N11, N3, N10assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Current node is N13. From N13, legal moves are to N11, N3, or N10.  \n- Moving to N11: next player faces N11, which has edges to N1 and N5. From there, opponent can move to N1 or N5.  \n  - N1 leads to N5 or N4 or N6; N5 leads to N7; N4 to N0 (loss); N6 has no outgoing.  \n  - This creates a chain that eventually leads to a terminal node.  \n- Moving to N3: N3 → N11, then to N1 or N5. Again, opponent can continue.  \n- Moving to N10: N10 → N12 (terminal, opponent loses immediately).  \n\nThus, moving to N10 causes opponent to face a node with no outgoing edges (N12), so opponent loses. This is an immediate win.  \nTherefore, N10 is the best move.</reason>\n<answer>N10</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Current node is N13. From N13, legal moves are to N11, N3, or N10.  \n- Moving to N11: next player faces N11, which has edges to N1 and N5. From there, opponent can move to N1 or N5.  \n  - N1 leads to N5 or N4 or N6; N5 leads to N7; N4 to N0 (loss); N6 has no outgoing.  \n  - This creates a chain that eventually leads to a terminal node.  \n- Moving to N3: N3 → N11, then to N1 or N5. Again, opponent can continue.  \n- Moving to N10: N10 → N12 (terminal, opponent loses immediately).  \n\nThus, moving to N10 causes opponent to face a node with no outgoing edges (N12), so opponent loses. This is an immediate win.  \nTherefore, N10 is the best move.</reason>\n<answer>N10</answer>"}]
