[2026-08-18 12:47:47] [agentic_pipeline.py (561)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 1863312] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. After you move to a destination, the opponent acts from that destination. If that destination has no outgoing edges, the opponent loses. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N2\n\nDirected graph:\nN9 -> N1, N0\nN8 -> N9, N4\nN1: no outgoing edges\nN2 -> N7, N5\nN7 -> N5, N8\nN6: no outgoing edges\nN4: no outgoing edges\nN0 -> N4, N3\nN5 -> N6\nN3: no outgoing edges\n\nLegal moves: N7, N5assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Current node is N2. From N2, legal moves are to N7 or N5.  \n- Moving to N7: next player is at N7, which has edges to N5 and N8.  \n  - If opponent goes to N5, they reach N6 (no outgoing edges) → opponent loses.  \n  - If opponent goes to N8, they go to N9 → N1 or N4; both lead to terminal nodes (N1 and N4 have no outgoing edges), so opponent loses.  \n  So from N7, opponent is forced into a losing position regardless.  \n- Moving to N5: next player is at N5, which goes to N6 (no outgoing edges) → opponent loses immediately.  \n\nBoth moves lead to opponent losing, but moving to N5 causes immediate loss for opponent. Moving to N7 gives opponent a choice but still loses. However, N5 leads to immediate win. Thus, N5 is better.  \nFinal choice: N5.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Current node is N2. From N2, legal moves are to N7 or N5.  \n- Moving to N7: next player is at N7, which has edges to N5 and N8.  \n  - If opponent goes to N5, they reach N6 (no outgoing edges) → opponent loses.