 - From N0, opponent can go to N4 or N1.  \n    - If to N4: opponent moves to N4 → N7 or N8 (both dead ends), so opponent loses.  \n    - If to N1: opponent moves to N5 or N2.  \n      - N5 is a dead end → opponent loses.  \n      - N2 → N9 or N6 → both lead to N9 (dead end) or N6 → N9 (dead end). So opponent eventually loses.  \n  So from N0, opponent is forced into a losing position.  \n- Moving to N4: next player faces N4 → N7 or N8 (both dead ends), so opponent loses immediately.  \n\nBoth moves lead to opponent losing, but moving to N4 causes immediate opponent loss. Thus, N4 is better.  \n</reason>  \n<answer>N4</answer>"}]
