nt node: N8\n\nDirected graph:\nN2: no outgoing edges\nN1: no outgoing edges\nN5 -> N2, N0\nN3: no outgoing edges\nN7: no outgoing edges\nN9 -> N1, N2\nN4 -> N5\nN0 -> N9, N3\nN8 -> N5, N6, N4\nN6 -> N7\n\nLegal moves: N5, N6, N4assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Current node is N8. From N8, legal moves are to N5, N6, or N4.  \n- Moving to N5: next player is at N5, which has outgoing edges to N2 and N0.  \n  - From N5, opponent can go to N2 (dead end) or N0.  \n    - If to N2: opponent loses → we win.  \n    - If to N0: opponent moves to N9 or N3.  \n      - N9 → N1 or N2 (both dead ends) → opponent loses.  \n      - N3 → dead end → opponent loses.  \n    So from N5, opponent has no winning move — they lose eventually.  \n- Moving to N6: next player goes to N7 (dead end) → opponent loses immediately.  \n- Moving to N4: next player goes to N5 → same as above, opponent eventually loses.  \n\nAll moves lead to opponent losing. But we want to maximize outcome. N6 leads to immediate opponent loss (N7 has no outgoing edges). This is optimal.  \n</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Current node is N8. From N8, legal moves are to N5, N6, or N4.  \n- Moving to N5: next player is at N5, which has outgoing edges to N2 and N0.  \n  - From N5, opponent can go to N2 (dead end) or N0.  \n    - If to N2: opponent loses → we win.  \n    - If to N0: opponent moves to N9 or N3.  \n      - N9 → N1 or N2 (both dead ends) → opponent loses.  \n      - N3 → dead end → opponent loses.  \n    So from N5, opponent has no winning move — they lose eventually.  \n- Moving to N6: next player goes to N7 (dead end) → opponent loses immediately.  \n- Moving to N4: next player goes to N5 → same as above, opponent eventually loses.  \n\nAll moves lead to opponent losing. But we want to maximize outcome. N6 leads to immediate opponent loss (N7 has no outgoing edges). This is optimal.  \n</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. After you move to a destination, the opponent acts from that destination. If that destination has no outgoing edges, the opponent loses. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N8\n\nDirected graph:\nN2: no outgoing edges\nN1: no outgoing edges\nN5 -> N2, N0\nN3: no outgoing edges\nN7: no outgoing edges\nN9 -> N1, N2\nN4 -> N5\nN0 -> N9, N3\nN8 -> N5, N6, N4\nN6 -> N7\n\nLegal moves: N5, N6, N4assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Current node is N8. From N8, legal moves are to N5, N6, or N4. We analyze each:\n\n- Move to N5: Next player is at N5, which has edges to N2 and N0. From N5, opponent can go to N2 (terminal) or N0. \n  - If to N2: opponent loses → we win.\n  - If to N0: opponent moves to N9 or N3. \n    - N9 → N1 or N2 (both terminal → opponent loses).\n    - N3 → terminal → opponent loses.\n  - So from N5, opponent eventually loses regardless. So moving to N5 is winning.\n\n- Move to N6: Next player is at N6 → goes to N7 (terminal), so opponent loses → we win.\n\n- Move to N4: Next player is at N4 → goes to N5. Then opponent plays from N5 (same as above), and eventually loses.\n\nAll moves lead to opponent losing. But we want to maximize outcome. Since all are winning, we choose one that gives best control. N6 leads directly to terminal (N7) in one step — immediate win. This is optimal.\n\nThus, best move is to N6.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Current node is N8. From N8, legal moves are to N5, N6, or N4. We analyze each:\n\n- Move to N5: Next player is at N5, which has edges to N2 and N0. From N5, opponent can go 