nd N5.  \n  - From N0, opponent can go to N9 (losing) or N5.  \n  - If to N5, then N5 → N4 or N2.  \n    - N4 ends game (opponent loses).  \n    - N2 → N8 (opponent loses).  \n  - So from N5, opponent can force a win.  \n- Moving to N7: next player faces N7 → N1 (no outgoing edges), so opponent loses immediately. This is a winning move.  \n- Moving to N3: next player faces N3 → N2 or N0.  \n  - N2 → N8 (opponent loses).  \n  - N0 → N9 or N5 (leads to continuation).  \n  - So opponent can choose N2 and win.  \n\nThus, moving to N7 immediately ends the game with opponent losing. This is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>"}]
