[2026-08-18 13:27:17] [agentic_pipeline.py (561)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 1863312] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. After you move to a destination, the opponent acts from that destination. If that destination has no outgoing edges, the opponent loses. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN9: no outgoing edges\nN10 -> N2\nN5: no outgoing edges\nN11 -> N12, N3\nN8 -> N1, N13\nN13 -> N6, N5\nN4 -> N10, N0\nN12 -> N1, N7\nN3 -> N9, N0\nN2 -> N11, N8\nN0 -> N5\nN7: no outgoing edges\nN1: no outgoing edges\nN6: no outgoing edges\n\nLegal moves: N10, N0assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Current node is N4. From N4, legal moves are to N10 or N0.  \n- Moving to N10: next player faces N10 → N2. From N2, moves to N11 or N8.  \n  - N11 → N12 or N3; N12 → N1 or N7; N3 → N9 or N0.  \n  - Eventually, paths lead to dead ends (N9, N5, N1, N7, N6, N1) or loops.  \n  - But if we go N4 → N0 → N5 (dead end), opponent loses immediately.  \n- Moving to N0 → N5 (dead end), opponent loses.  \nThus, moving to N0 leads to opponent having no move (since N5 has no outgoing edges).  \nThis is a winning move. So, choose N0.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Current node is N4. From N4, legal moves are to N10 or N0.  \n- Moving to N10: next player faces N10 → N2. From N2, moves to N11 or N8.  \n  - N11 → N12 or N3; N12 → N1 or N7; N3 → N9 or N0.  \n  - Eventually, paths lead to dead ends (N9, N5, N1, N7, N6, N1) or loops.  \n  - But if we go N4 → N0 → N5 (dead end), opponent loses immediately.  \n- Moving to N0 → N5 (dead end), opponent loses.  \nThus, moving to N0 leads to opponent having no move (since N5 has no outgoing edges).  \nThis is a winning move. So, choose N0.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. After you move to a destination, the opponent acts from that destination. If that destination has no outgoing edges, the opponent loses. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN9: no outgoing edges\nN10 -> N2\nN5: no outgoing edges\nN11 -> N12, N3\nN8 -> N1, N13\nN13 -> N6, N5\nN4 -> N10, N0\nN12 -> N1, N7\nN3 -> N9, N0\nN2 -> N11, N8\nN0 -> N5\nN7: no outgoing edges\nN1: no outgoing edges\nN6: no outgoing edges\n\nLegal moves: N10, N0assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N4, legal moves are to N10 or N0.  \n- Moving to N10: leads to N2, then from N2 to N11 or N8.  \n  - N11 → N12 or N3; N12 → N1 or N7 (N7 and N1 are terminal, so opponent loses).  \n  - N3 → N9 or N0; N9 is terminal, so opponent loses.  \n  - N8 → N1 or N13; N13 → N6 or N5 (both terminal).  \n  So from N2, opponent can be forced into a terminal node.  \n- Moving to N0: leads to N5 (terminal), so opponent loses immediately.  \n\nThus, moving to N0 wins immediately. N10 leads to a longer game with possible opponent moves, but N0 results in immediate opponent loss. Therefore, N0 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N4, legal moves are to N10 or N0.  \n- Moving to N10: leads to N2, then from N2 to N11 or N8.  \n  - N11 → N12 or N3; N12 → N1 or N7 (N7 and N1 are terminal, so opponent loses).  \n  - N3 → N9 or N0; N9 is terminal, so opponent loses.  \n  - N8 → N1 or N13; N13 → N6 or N5 (both terminal).  \n  So from N2, opponent can be forced into a terminal node.  \n- Moving to N0: leads to N5 (terminal), so opponent loses immediately.  \n\nThus, moving to N0 wins immediately. N10 leads to a longer game with possible opponent moves, but N0 results in immediate opponent loss. Therefore, N0 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. After you move to a destination, the opponent acts from that destination. If that destination has no outgoing edges, the opponent loses. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN9: no outgoing edges\nN10 -> N2\nN5: no outgoing edges\nN11 -> N12, N3\nN8 -> N1, N13\nN13 -> N6, N5\nN4 -> N10, N0\nN12 -> N1, N7\nN3 -> N9, N0\nN2 -> N11, N8\nN0 -> N5\nN7: no outgoing edges\nN1: no outgoing edges\nN6: no outgoing edges\n\nLegal moves: N10, N0assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N4, legal moves are to N10 or N0.  \n- Moving to N10: leads to N2, then from N2 to N11 or N8.  \n  - N11 → N12 or N3; N12 → N1 or N7 (N7 and N1 are terminal, opponent loses).  \n  - N3 → N9 or N0; N9 is terminal.  \n  - N8 → N1 or N13; N13 → N6 or N5 (both terminal).  \n  - So from N2, opponent can force a win by going to N8 → N13 → N6 (terminal).  \n  - Alternatively, N2 → N11 → N12 → N1 (terminal).  \n  - Either way, opponent can force a win.  \n- Moving to N0: leads to N5 (terminal), so opponent loses immediately.  \nThus, moving to N0 wins the game.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>", "episode_score