 "<reason>Current node is N2. From N2, legal moves are to N0, N7, or N4.  \n- Moving to N0: leads to N8, which has edges to N3, N5, N6. All of these end in no outgoing edges (N3, N6) or lead to N1 (no outgoing edges). So from N8, opponent will eventually lose.  \n- Moving to N7: leads to N9, which has no outgoing edges → opponent loses immediately.  \n- Moving to N4: leads to N8, same as above.  \n\nBoth N0 and N4 lead to N8, which forces opponent into a losing position. But N7 leads directly to N9, an immediate loss for opponent. So moving to N7 wins immediately. Thus, best move is N7.</reason>  \n<answer>N7</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Current node is N2. From N2, legal moves are to N0, N7, or N4.  \n- Moving to N0: leads to N8, which has edges to N3, N5, N6. All of these end in no outgoing edges (N3, N6) or lead to N1 (no outgoing edges). So from N8, opponent will eventually lose.  \n- Moving to N7: leads to N9, which has no outgoing edges → opponent loses immediately.  \n- Moving to N4: leads to N8, same as above.  \n\nBoth N0 and N4 lead to N8, which forces opponent into a losing position. But N7 leads directly to N9, an immediate loss for opponent. So moving to N7 wins immediately. Thus, best move is N7.</reason>  \n<answer>N7</answer>"}]
