[2026-08-18 13:38:40] [agentic_pipeline.py (561)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 1863312] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. After you move to a destination, the opponent acts from that destination. If that destination has no outgoing edges, the opponent loses. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N7\n\nDirected graph:\nN5: no outgoing edges\nN8: no outgoing edges\nN2: no outgoing edges\nN6: no outgoing edges\nN0 -> N3, N4\nN7 -> N1, N0\nN3 -> N9, N8\nN9 -> N5, N4\nN4 -> N5\nN1 -> N6, N2\n\nLegal moves: N1, N0assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Current node is N7. From N7, legal moves are to N1 or N0.  \n- Moving to N1: next player faces N1, which has edges to N6 and N2 (both dead ends). So from N1, opponent must move to N6 or N2, both of which have no outgoing edges. Thus, opponent loses immediately.  \n- Moving to N0: next player faces N0, which has edges to N3 and N4.  \n  - From N3: edges to N9 and N8. N8 is a dead end, N9 to N5 and N4.  \n  - From N4: to N5 (dead end).  \n  This leads to a longer game, but the opponent can eventually force a win by navigating to N5 or N8.  \nThus, moving to N1 immediately forces opponent into a dead end. Moving to N0 gives opponent a chance to survive longer, but not win. Therefore, N1 is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Current node is N7. From N7, legal moves are to N1 or N0.  \n- Moving to N1: next player faces N1, which has edges to N6 and N2 (both dead ends). So from N1, opponent must move to N6 or N2, both of which have no outgoing edges. Thus, opponent loses imme