[2026-08-18 13:44:07] [agentic_pipeline.py (561)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 1863312] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. After you move to a destination, the opponent acts from that destination. If that destination has no outgoing edges, the opponent loses. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N0\n\nDirected graph:\nN3: no outgoing edges\nN2 -> N8, N4\nN7 -> N3, N6\nN0 -> N1, N7\nN6: no outgoing edges\nN4: no outgoing edges\nN1 -> N2, N8\nN8 -> N9, N5\nN5 -> N3\nN9: no outgoing edges\n\nLegal moves: N1, N7assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N0, the legal moves are to N1 or N7. We analyze both options to determine which leads to a winning position.\n\nIf we move to N1:\n- From N1, opponent can go to N2 or N8.\n  - If opponent goes to N2: then we can go to N8 or N4. \n    - N4 has no outgoing edges → opponent loses if we go to N4.\n    - N8 leads to N9 or N5; N5 leads to N3 (no outgoing edges), so opponent loses.\n  - If opponent goes to N8: leads to N9 or N5; N9 has no outgoing edges → opponent loses immediately.\nThus, from N1, opponent is forced into a losing position regardless.\n\nIf we move to N7:\n- Opponent can go to N3 or N6, both of which have no outgoing edges → opponent loses immediately.\n\nThus, moving to N7 causes opponent to lose immediately. This is a winning move.\n\nTherefore, the best immediate move is to N7.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N0, the legal moves are to N1 or N7. We analyze both options to determine which leads to a winning position.\n\nIf we move to N1:\n- From N1, opponent can go to N2 or N8.\n  - If opponent goes to N2: then we can go to N8 or N4. \n    - N4 has no outgoing edges → opponent loses if we go to N4.\n    - N8 leads to N9 or N5; N5 leads to N3 (no outgoing edges), so opponent loses.\n  - If opponent goes to N8: leads to N9 or N5; N9 has no outgoing edges → opponent loses immediately.\nThus, from N1, opponent is forced into a losing position regardless.\n\nIf we move to N7:\n- Opponent can go to N3 or N6, both of which have no outgoing edges → opponent loses immediately.\n\nThus, moving to N7 causes opponent to lose immediately. This is a winning move.\n\nTherefore, the best immediate move is to N7.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. After you move to a destination, the opponent acts from that destination. If that destination has no outgoing edges, the opponent loses. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N0\n\nDirected graph:\nN3: no outgoing edges\nN2 -> N8, N4\nN7 -> N3, N6\nN0 -> N1, N7\nN6: no outgoing edges\nN4: no outgoing edges\nN1 -> N2, N8\nN8 -> N9, N5\nN5 -> N3\nN9: no outgoing edges\n\nLegal moves: N1, N7assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N0, the legal moves are to N1 or N7. We analyze both:\n\n- Move to N1: Then opponent is at N1. From N1, opponent can go to N2 or N8.\n  - If opponent goes to N2: then we are at N2, which has moves to N8 or N4. \n    - If we go to N8: opponent goes to N9 or N5. \n      - N9 has no outgoing edges → opponent loses → we win.\n      - N5 → N3 (no outgoing edges) → opponent loses → we win.\n    - If we go to N4: no outgoing edges → opponent loses → we win.\n  - If opponent goes to N8: then we are at N8 → moves to N9 or N5 → both end in opponent losing → we win.\n  So from N1, we can force a win.\n\n- Move to N7: opponent goes to N3 or N6, both of which have no outgoing edges → opponent loses immediately → we win.\n\nThus, both moves win, but moving to N7 immediately ends the game with opponent losing. This is optimal.\n\nTherefore, the best move is to N7.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N0, the legal moves are to N1 or N7. We analyze both:\n\n- Move to N1: Then opponent is at N1. From N1, opponent can go to N2 or N8.\n  - If opponent goes to N2: then we are at N2, which has moves to N8 or N4. \n    - If we go to N8: opponent goes to N9 or N5. \n      - N9 has no outgoing edges → opponent loses → we win.\n      - N5 → N3 (no outgoing edges) → opponent loses → we win.\n    - If we go to N4: no outgoing edges → opponent loses → we win.\n  - If opponent goes to N8: then we are at N8 → moves to N9 or N5 → both end in opponent losing → we win.\n  So from N1, we can force a win.\n\n- Move to N7: opponent goes to N3 or N6, both of which have no outgoing edges → opponent loses immediately → we win.\n\nThus, both moves win, but moving to N7 immediately ends the game with opponent losing. This is optimal.\n\nTherefore, the best move is to N7.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. After you move to a destination, the opponent acts from that destination. If that destination has no outgoing edges, the opponent loses. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results