[2026-08-18 13:49:33] [agentic_pipeline.py (561)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 1863312] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. After you move to a destination, the opponent acts from that destination. If that destination has no outgoing edges, the opponent loses. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N9\n\nDirected graph:\nN2 -> N1, N5\nN6: no outgoing edges\nN5 -> N7\nN9 -> N1, N3, N0\nN7: no outgoing edges\nN1 -> N5\nN4: no outgoing edges\nN3 -> N2, N4, N6\nN8: no outgoing edges\nN0 -> N8\n\nLegal moves: N1, N3, N0assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N9, the legal moves are to N1, N3, or N0. We analyze each:\n\n- Move to N1: Then opponent is at N1, which has an edge to N5. Opponent moves to N5, then to N7 (dead end). So opponent loses → we win.\n\n- Move to N3: Opponent at N3 has edges to N2, N4, N6. All lead to dead ends or loops. But N2 → N1 → N5 → N7 (dead end), so opponent can go N3 → N2 → N1 → N5 → N7, opponent loses. So we win.\n\n- Move to N0: Opponent at N0 → N8 (dead end), opponent loses → we win.\n\nAll moves lead to opponent losing. But we want to maximize outcome. Since all result in win, any is valid. Choose N0 as it is a direct dead-end move, simplest and guarantees win.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N9, the legal moves are to N1, N3, or N0. We analyze each:\n\n- Move to N1: Then opponent is at N1, which has an edge to N5. Opponent moves to N5, then to N7 (dead end). So opponent loses → we win.\n\n- Move to N3: Opponent at N3 has edges to N2, N4, N6. All lead to dead ends or loops. But N2 → N1 → N5 → N7 (dead end), so opponent can go N3 → N2 → N1 → N5 → N7, opponent loses. So we win.\n\n- Move to N0: Opponent at N0 → N8 (dead end), opponent loses → we win.\n\nAll moves lead to opponent losing. But we want to maximize outcome. Since all result in win, any is valid. Choose N0 as it is a direct dead-end move, simplest and guarantees win.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. After you move to a destination, the opponent acts from that destination. If that destination has no outgoing edges, the opponent loses. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N9\n\nDirected graph:\nN2 -> N1, N5\nN6: no outgoing edges\nN5 -> N7\nN9 -> N1, N3, N0\nN7: no outgoing edges\nN1 -> N5\nN4: no outgoing edges\nN3 -> N2, N4, N6\nN8: no outgoing edges\nN0 -> N8\n\nLegal moves: N1, N3, N0assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N9, the legal moves are to N1, N3, or N0. We analyze each:\n\n- Move to N1: Then opponent is at N1, which has an edge to N5. Opponent moves to N5, then to N7 (terminal). Opponent loses → we win.\n\n- Move to N3: Opponent at N3 has edges to N2, N4, N6. All lead to terminal or recursive paths. \n  - If opponent goes to N2 → N1 → N5 → N7 (opponent loses).\n  - If to N4 → terminal (opponent loses).\n  - If to N6 → terminal (opponent loses).\n  So opponent loses regardless → we win.\n\n- Move to N0: Opponent at N0 → N8 (terminal), opponent loses → we win.\n\nAll moves lead to opponent losing. Any move wins. Choose one that maximizes outcome — all are equivalent. Pick N1 as it is a central node with clear path.</reason>\n<answ