[2026-08-18 14:08:23] [agentic_pipeline.py (561)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 1863312] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. After you move to a destination, the opponent acts from that destination. If that destination has no outgoing edges, the opponent loses. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN1 -> N8\nN8: no outgoing edges\nN5 -> N1, N3\nN7 -> N9\nN4 -> N7, N0, N5\nN0 -> N7, N5\nN2: no outgoing edges\nN3: no outgoing edges\nN6: no outgoing edges\nN9 -> N2, N6\n\nLegal moves: N7, N0, N5assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N4, legal moves are to N7, N0, or N5. We analyze each:\n\n- Move to N7: goes to N9, then opponent moves to N2 or N6 (both terminal). Opponent loses immediately. So we win.\n\n- Move to N0: goes to N7 or N5. From N7, opponent goes to N9, then to N2 or N6 — opponent loses. So we win.\n\n- Move to N5: goes to N1 or N3. N3 has no outgoing edges → opponent loses immediately. So we win.\n\nAll moves lead to opponent losing eventually. But we want to maximize outcome. Since all moves lead to win, any is valid. However, moving to N5 leads to immediate opponent loss at N3, which is stronger than others. Thus, N5 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N4, legal moves are to N7, N0, or N5. We analyze each:\n\n- Move to N7: goes to N9, then opponent moves to N2 or N6 (both terminal). Opponent loses immediately. So we win.\n\n- Move to N0: goes to N7 or N5. From N7, opponent goes to N9, then to N2 or N6 — opponent loses. So we win.\n\n- Move to N5: goes to N1 or N3. N3 has no outgoing edges → opponent loses immediately. So we win.\n\nAll moves lead to opponent losing eventually. But we want to maximize outcome. Since all moves lead to win, any is valid. However, moving to N5 leads to immediate opponent loss at N3, which is stronger than others. Thus, N5 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. After you move to a destination, the opponent acts from that destination. If that destination has no outgoing edges, the opponent loses. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN1 -> N8\nN8: no outgoing edges\nN5 -> N1, N3\nN7 -> N9\nN4 -> N7, N0, N5\nN0 -> N7, N5\nN2: no outgoing edges\nN3: no outgoing edges\nN6: no outgoing edges\nN9 -> N2, N6\n\nLegal moves: N7, N0, N5assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N4, legal moves are to N7, N0, or N5. We analyze each:\n\n- Move to N7: goes to N7 → N9 → N2 or N6. N2 and N6 have no outgoing edges, so the opponent loses immediately. So this is a winning move.\n\n- Move to N0: goes to N0 → N7 or N5. From N7 → N9 → N2 or N6 (opponent loses). From N5 → N1 → N8 (N8 has no outgoing edges, opponent loses). So both paths lead to opponent losing. Winning move.\n\n- Move to N5: goes to N5 → N1 → N8 (opponent loses). Winning move.\n\nAll moves lead to opponent losing. Any move wins. Choose one that maximizes outcome — all are equivalent. Pick N7 as it leads directly to N9, which forces opponent into a terminal node.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>", "episode_score": 1.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N4, legal moves are to N7, N0, or 