nt has no winning move.  \n- Moving to N9: goes to N8 → N8 leads to N2 or N13.  \n  - N2 → N13 → N7 or N10 → N0 or N12 (dead ends).  \n  - N13 → N7 or N10 → same.  \n  All paths eventually lead to dead ends.  \n\nAll moves lead to opponent losing eventually. But moving to N6 directly leads to N4 (dead end for opponent) — immediate win. This is the most direct and guaranteed win. Thus, N6 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>"}]
