[2026-08-18 14:23:42] [agentic_pipeline.py (561)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 1863312] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. After you move to a destination, the opponent acts from that destination. If that destination has no outgoing edges, the opponent loses. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN7: no outgoing edges\nN3: no outgoing edges\nN8 -> N4\nN0 -> N11, N12\nN1 -> N3\nN2: no outgoing edges\nN11: no outgoing edges\nN13 -> N0, N5\nN5 -> N1\nN10 -> N11, N13\nN12 -> N2\nN4 -> N5, N10\nN6 -> N8, N9\nN9 -> N3, N7\n\nLegal moves: N8, N9assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N6, legal moves are to N8 or N9.  \n- Moving to N8: goes to N4, then opponent can go to N5 or N10.  \n  - If to N5: goes to N1, then to N3 (opponent loses).  \n  - If to N10: goes to N11 or N13.  \n    - N11 ends game (opponent loses).  \n    - N13 → N0 or N5 → N1 → N3 (opponent loses).  \n  So from N4, opponent has no winning path — they lose.  \n- Moving to N9: goes to N3 or N7, both of which have no outgoing edges → opponent loses immediately.  \n\nBoth moves lead to opponent losing, but moving to N9 immediately ends the game with opponent losing. Thus, N9 is better because it ends the game instantly.  \n</reason>  \n<answer>N9</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N6, legal moves are to N8 or N9.  \n- Moving to N8: goes to N4, then opponent can go to N5 or N10.  \n  - If to N5: goes to N1, then to N3 (opponent loses).  \n  - If to N10: goes to N11 or N13.  \n    - N11 ends game (opponent loses).  \n    - N13 → N0 or N5 → N1 → N3 (opponent loses).  \n  So from N4, opponent has no winning path — they lose.  \n- Moving to N9: goes to N3 or N7, both of which have no outgoing edges → opponent loses immediately.  \n\nBoth moves lead to opponent losing, but moving to N9 immediately ends the game with opponent losing. Thus, N9 is better because it ends the game instantly.  \n</reason>  \n<answer>N9</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. After you move to a destination, the opponent acts from that destination. If that destination has no outgoing edges, the opponent loses. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN7: no outgoing edges\nN3: no outgoing edges\nN8 -> N4\nN0 -> N11, N12\nN1 -> N3\nN2: no outgoing edges\nN11: no outgoing edges\nN13 -> N0, N5\nN5 -> N1\nN10 -> N11, N13\nN12 -> N2\nN4 -> N5, N10\nN6 -> N8, N9\nN9 -> N3, N7\n\nLegal moves: N8, N9assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N6, legal moves are to N8 or N9.  \n- Moving to N8: goes to N4, then opponent can go to N5 or N10.  \n  - If to N5: goes to N1, then to N3 (opponent loses).  \n  - If to N10: goes to N11 or N13.  \n    - N11 ends game (opponent loses).  \n    - N13 → N0 or N5 → N1 → N3 (opponent loses).  \n  So from N4, opponent eventually loses.  \n- Moving to N9: goes to N3 or N7, both of which have no outgoing edges → opponent loses immediately.  \n\nThus, moving to N9 wins immediately. N9 leads to a terminal node for the opponent. This is better than N8, which requires more steps. Choose N9.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N6, legal m