e to N9: Opponent is at N9, which has edges to N4 and N2 — both dead ends. So opponent loses immediately.\n\nThus, moving to N9 causes opponent to lose immediately. This is better than N0, where opponent still has options.\n\nTherefore, the best move is to N9.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>"}]
